Work-section guidance:
- Prioritize evidence of implementation, production delivery, reliability,
  debugging, testing, ownership, judgment, and collaboration when supported.
- Put the strongest target-role accomplishment first and use later bullets to
  demonstrate different capabilities.
- Distinguish maintaining, integrating, testing, implementing, leading, and
  owning; do not inflate ordinary work into architecture or leadership.
- Every role must contain at least one bullet built around a decision, a
  tradeoff, or an obstacle the candidate worked through, carrying no metric at
  all. A role whose every bullet ends in a statistic reads as machine output,
  not as work someone did.
- Scale verb strength to scope per the verb ladder. Five endpoints, one script,
  or one feature is tier-1 work — "built", not "architected".
